{
  "id": "layer-event-corollaries",
  "goals": [
    "a corollary of a WASI command's executable over the layer events of the Linux shim",
    "InRange ls → Counts args ls (q.core.x 0)",
    "a trapped run of main excluded by a condition on the layer events",
    "the shape of the layer events: the calls, their counts, and their flags",
    "List.Forall₂ Mirrors events groups with ls = groups.flatten",
    "∃ q ls, … ∧ (InRange ls → Counts …) shown satisfiable by a witness",
    "cases on Images whose index is [] ++ []",
    "the loader's memory and the initial stack of the witness of an executable's corollary",
    "a WASI call that the shim answers with a loop of Linux calls, such as random_get with getrandom until the buffer is full",
    "a short getrandom read in a corollary over layer events",
    "the weakest condition on Linux's results under which a corollary holds",
    "the output length of a layer event, which an image leaves free",
    "a write whose count argument is free of its input in a statement over layer events"
  ],
  "modules": [
    "Demos.RandomHistogram.NativeCounts",
    "Demos.RandomChoice.NativeChoices",
    "Verified.Shim.Trace"
  ],
